#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/__riscv_flush_icache.3:24
msgid ""
"B<__riscv_flush_icache>()  enforces ordering between stores and instruction "
"cache fetches."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/__riscv_flush_icache.3:29
msgid ""
"The range of addresses over which ordering is enforced is specified by "
"I<start> and I<end>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/__riscv_flush_icache.3:46
msgid ""
"The I<flags> argument controls the extent of this ordering, with the default "
"behavior (a I<flags> value of 0)  being to enforce the fence on all threads "
"in the current process.  Setting the B<SYS_RISCV_FLUSH_ICACHE_LOCAL> bit "
"allows users to indicate that enforcing ordering on only the current thread "
"is necessary.  All other bits in I<flags> are reserved."
msgstr ""

