#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:70
msgid ""
"B<chmod>()  changes the mode of the file specified whose pathname is given "
"in I<path>, which is dereferenced if it is a symbolic link."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:74
msgid ""
"B<fchmod>()  changes the mode of the file referred to by the open file "
"descriptor I<fd>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:79
msgid ""
"The new file mode is specified in I<mode>, which is a bit mask created by "
"ORing together zero or more of the following:"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:79
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<S_ISUID>  (04000)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:83
msgid "set-user-ID (set process effective user ID on B<execve>(2))"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:83
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<S_ISGID>  (02000)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:93
msgid ""
"set-group-ID (set process effective group ID on B<execve>(2); mandatory "
"locking, as described in B<fcntl>(2); take a new file's group from parent "
"directory, as described in B<chown>(2)  and B<mkdir>(2))"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:93
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<S_ISVTX>  (01000)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:97
msgid "sticky bit (restricted deletion flag, as described in B<unlink>(2))"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:97
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<S_IRUSR>  (00400)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:100
msgid "read by owner"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:100
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<S_IWUSR>  (00200)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:103
msgid "write by owner"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:103
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<S_IXUSR>  (00100)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:107
msgid ""
"execute/search by owner (\"search\" applies for directories, and means that "
"entries within the directory can be accessed)"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:107
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<S_IRGRP>  (00040)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:110
msgid "read by group"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:110
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<S_IWGRP>  (00020)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:113
msgid "write by group"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:113
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<S_IXGRP>  (00010)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:116
msgid "execute/search by group"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:116
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<S_IROTH>  (00004)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:119
msgid "read by others"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:119
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<S_IWOTH>  (00002)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:122
msgid "write by others"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<S_IXOTH>  (00001)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:125
msgid "execute/search by others"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:130
msgid ""
"The effective UID of the calling process must match the owner of the file, "
"or the process must be privileged (Linux: it must have the B<CAP_FOWNER> "
"capability)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:139
msgid ""
"If the calling process is not privileged (Linux: does not have the "
"B<CAP_FSETID> capability), and the group of the file does not match the "
"effective group ID of the process or one of its supplementary group IDs, the "
"B<S_ISGID> bit will be turned off, but this will not cause an error to be "
"returned."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:151
msgid ""
"As a security measure, depending on the filesystem, the set-user-ID and "
"set-group-ID execution bits may be turned off if a file is written.  (On "
"Linux, this occurs if the writing process does not have the B<CAP_FSETID> "
"capability.)  On some filesystems, only the superuser can set the sticky "
"bit, which may have a special meaning.  For the sticky bit, and for "
"set-user-ID and set-group-ID bits on directories, see B<inode>(7)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:159
msgid ""
"On NFS filesystems, restricting the permissions will immediately influence "
"already open files, because the access control is done on the server, but "
"open files are maintained by the client.  Widening the permissions may be "
"delayed for other clients if attribute caching is enabled on them."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:159
#, no-wrap
msgid "fchmodat()"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:165
msgid ""
"The B<fchmodat>()  system call operates in exactly the same way as "
"B<chmod>(), except for the differences described here."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:175
msgid ""
"If I<path> is relative, then it is interpreted relative to the directory "
"referred to by the file descriptor I<dirfd> (rather than relative to the "
"current working directory of the calling process, as is done by B<chmod>()  "
"for a relative pathname)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:187
msgid ""
"If I<path> is relative and I<dirfd> is the special value B<AT_FDCWD>, then "
"I<path> is interpreted relative to the current working directory of the "
"calling process (like B<chmod>())."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:196
msgid "I<flags> can either be 0, or include the following flags:"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:196
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<AT_EMPTY_PATH> (since Linux 6.6)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:226
msgid ""
"If I<path> is a symbolic link, do not dereference it: instead operate on the "
"link itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/chmod.2:231
msgid "See B<openat>(2)  for an explanation of the need for B<fchmodat>()."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
